{"id":"040766e915f9aff3","group":"58","path":"58/batch11/58-df-weak-topology.md","title":"Weak Topology","display":"df-weak-topology — Weak Topology","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-weak-topology","aliases":["58-df-weak-topology","Weak Topology"],"display":"df-weak-topology — Weak Topology","depends_on":["[[../batch16/58-df-dual-space.md]]","[[../batch05/58-df-normed-space.md]]","[[../batch14/58-df-topology.md]]","[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]","[[../batch05/58-df-surjective.md]]","[[../batch13/58-df-zfc-rel-directed-set.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-weak-topology"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-weak-topology</span><span>Weak Topology</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-weak-topology — Weak Topology"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"c740b73b26d2ecf9\" href=\"?note=c740b73b26d2ecf9\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-dual-space.md\">../batch16/58-df-dual-space.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"bdbbe5a00af04978\" href=\"?note=bdbbe5a00af04978\" title=\"../batch05/58-df-normed-space.md\">../batch05/58-df-normed-space.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"e7514bc4cefba4f2\" href=\"?note=e7514bc4cefba4f2\" title=\"../batch14/58-df-topology.md\">../batch14/58-df-topology.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"9f8cb046321ba311\" href=\"?note=9f8cb046321ba311\" title=\"../batch05/58-df-surjective.md\">../batch05/58-df-surjective.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"9f6ab9827c296452\" href=\"?note=9f6ab9827c296452\" title=\"../batch13/58-df-zfc-rel-directed-set.md\">../batch13/58-df-zfc-rel-directed-set.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X\">\\(X\\)</span> (normed space with designated scalar field <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"K_X\">\\(K_X\\)</span>), <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"D=X^*\">\\(D=X^*\\)</span> (continuous dual), and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\tau_K\">\\(\\tau_K\\)</span> (a topology on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"K_X\">\\(K_X\\)</span>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(I,\\preceq)\">\\((I,\\preceq)\\)</span> (directed set), <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"x:I\\to X\">\\(x:I\\to X\\)</span> (net), and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"x_0\\in X\">\\(x_0\\in X\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"J:X\\to X^{**}\">\\(J:X\\to X^{**}\\)</span> (canonical evaluation map)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{NormedSpace}_S,\\mathrm{Top},\\mathrm{Function},\\mathrm{Surjective}\">\\(\\mathrm{NormedSpace}_S,\\mathrm{Top},\\mathrm{Function},\\mathrm{Surjective}\\)</span> (upstream predicates)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcRelDirectedSet}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcRelDirectedSet}_S\\)</span> (directed-set predicate from dependency)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{WeakConvergence}_S,\\mathrm{WeakVectorTopology}_S,\\mathrm{CanonicalEmbedding}_S,\\mathrm{ReflexiveNormedSpace}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{WeakConvergence}_S,\\mathrm{WeakVectorTopology}_S,\\mathrm{CanonicalEmbedding}_S,\\mathrm{ReflexiveNormedSpace}_S\\)</span> (predicates defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}weak\\text{-}topology} \\vdash \\mathrm{WeakVectorTopology}_S(\\tau_w,X,D,\\tau_K)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{NormedSpace}_S(X)\\land D=X^*\\land\\mathrm{Top}(\\tau_K,K_X)\\land\\mathrm{Top}(\\tau_w,X)\\land\\forall f\\in D\\;\\forall O\\in\\tau_K\\;(f^{-1}[O]\\in\\tau_w)\\land\\forall\\tau\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{Top}(\\tau,X)\\land\\forall f\\in D\\;\\forall O\\in\\tau_K\\;(f^{-1}[O]\\in\\tau)\\to\\tau_w\\subseteq\\tau\\bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}weak\\text{-}topology} \\vdash \\mathrm{WeakVectorTopology}_S(\\tau_w,X,D,\\tau_K)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{NormedSpace}_S(X)\\land D=X^*\\land\\mathrm{Top}(\\tau_K,K_X)\\land\\mathrm{Top}(\\tau_w,X)\\land\\forall f\\in D\\;\\forall O\\in\\tau_K\\;(f^{-1}[O]\\in\\tau_w)\\land\\forall\\tau\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{Top}(\\tau,X)\\land\\forall f\\in D\\;\\forall O\\in\\tau_K\\;(f^{-1}[O]\\in\\tau)\\to\\tau_w\\subseteq\\tau\\bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}weak\\text{-}topology} \\vdash \\mathrm{WeakConvergence}_S(x,I,\\preceq,x_0,X,D,\\tau_K)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{NormedSpace}_S(X)\\land D=X^*\\land\\mathrm{Top}(\\tau_K,K_X)\\land\\mathrm{ZfcRelDirectedSet}_S(I,\\preceq)\\land\\mathrm{Function}(x,I,X)\\land x_0\\in X\\land\\forall f\\in D\\;\\forall O\\in\\tau_K\\;\\bigl(f(x_0)\\in O\\to\\exists i_0\\in I\\;\\forall i\\in I\\;(\\langle i_0,i\\rangle\\in\\preceq\\to f(x_i)\\in O)\\bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}weak\\text{-}topology} \\vdash \\mathrm{WeakConvergence}_S(x,I,\\preceq,x_0,X,D,\\tau_K)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{NormedSpace}_S(X)\\land D=X^*\\land\\mathrm{Top}(\\tau_K,K_X)\\land\\mathrm{ZfcRelDirectedSet}_S(I,\\preceq)\\land\\mathrm{Function}(x,I,X)\\land x_0\\in X\\land\\forall f\\in D\\;\\forall O\\in\\tau_K\\;\\bigl(f(x_0)\\in O\\to\\exists i_0\\in I\\;\\forall i\\in I\\;(\\langle i_0,i\\rangle\\in\\preceq\\to f(x_i)\\in O)\\bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}weak\\text{-}topology} \\vdash \\mathrm{CanonicalEmbedding}_S(J,X,X^{**})\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{Function}(J,X,X^{**})\\land\\forall x\\in X\\;\\forall f\\in X^*\\;(J(x)(f)=f(x))\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}weak\\text{-}topology} \\vdash \\mathrm{CanonicalEmbedding}_S(J,X,X^{**})\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{Function}(J,X,X^{**})\\land\\forall x\\in X\\;\\forall f\\in X^*\\;(J(x)(f)=f(x))\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}weak\\text{-}topology} \\vdash \\mathrm{ReflexiveNormedSpace}_S(X,J)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{NormedSpace}_S(X)\\land\\mathrm{CanonicalEmbedding}_S(J,X,X^{**})\\land\\mathrm{Surjective}(J,X,X^{**})\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}weak\\text{-}topology} \\vdash \\mathrm{ReflexiveNormedSpace}_S(X,J)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{NormedSpace}_S(X)\\land\\mathrm{CanonicalEmbedding}_S(J,X,X^{**})\\land\\mathrm{Surjective}(J,X,X^{**})\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Weak topology is characterized by both continuity of every <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"f\\in X^*\">\\(f\\in X^*\\)</span> and the displayed minimality clause.</li>\n<li>The predicate is named <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{WeakVectorTopology}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{WeakVectorTopology}_S\\)</span> to avoid collision with the CW-complex weak-topology predicate, which has different data and semantics.</li>\n<li>Net convergence now uses the canonical directed-relation predicate and relation membership, replacing an unproven local predicate name and infix use of an arbitrary set.</li>\n<li>Banach-Alaoglu: unit ball in <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X^*\">\\(X^*\\)</span> is weak* compact</li>\n<li>Reflexivity means surjectivity of the canonical embedding, not merely an informal equality of its image with <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X^{**}\">\\(X^{**}\\)</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Rudin, Functional Analysis</li>\n<li>Conway, A Course in Functional Analysis</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch16/58-df-dual-space.md","status":"resolved","id":"c740b73b26d2ecf9","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch16/58-df-dual-space.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch05/58-df-normed-space.md","status":"resolved","id":"bdbbe5a00af04978","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch05/58-df-normed-space.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch14/58-df-topology.md","status":"resolved","id":"e7514bc4cefba4f2","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch14/58-df-topology.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch05/58-df-surjective.md","status":"resolved","id":"9f8cb046321ba311","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch05/58-df-surjective.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch13/58-df-zfc-rel-directed-set.md","status":"resolved","id":"9f6ab9827c296452","anchor":"ref-6","targetAnchor":"","lo